            "review_title": "Review at Waterfall Dining Lounge",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nNew restaurant in Centara Mirage Resort, not to be confused with Waterfall Lounge\nJan 2022\nTried this restaurant on our vacation in Centara Mirage Resort, and we were so glad we did.\n\nDesign:\nIt looked beautiful from the outside, surrounded by a pool and was right below the infinity pool. The rocks leading up to and lining the entire interior of the restaurant, paired with wavy turquoise glass pieces on its ceiling was probably them going for an \"underwater cave\" kind of dining experience. The view from their full length glass windows were those of the two beautifully landscaped pools below, as well as the sea beyond. Quite a sight to behold.\n\nFood:\nFood-wise, definitely the best in the entire resort and probably this part of town. We had two consecutive meals here ever since we realised they were open (yea, they don't look bright from the outside so one might not notice that it's open). Fine dining at above average (but still rather affordable) prices. Exciting flavours that were well-executed across a variety of dishes - lobsters, foie gras, duck, barramundi, lamb chops, other seafood... beautifully plated too.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 22, 2022",
